{
 "segments": [
  {
   "text": "Case Twenty-Eight.",
   "start": 0.75,
   "end": 1.945,
   "pause": 0.6
  },
  {
   "text": "Truth and Fib Night.",
   "start": 2.545,
   "end": 3.91,
   "pause": 1.4
  },
  {
   "text": "Every year on the first of April, the village hall holds Truth and Fib Night. The rule is very simple, and everyone sticks to it all evening, because it's the whole point of the game. Whenever anyone says two things in a row, exactly one of them must be true, and exactly one must be a fib.",
   "start": 5.31,
   "end": 22.931,
   "pause": 0.85
  },
  {
   "text": "This year, the prize for the best fib of the night was a magnificent chocolate cake, baked by Jago Penhallow and decorated with a sugar fish. Halfway through the evening, the cake vanished from the prize table.",
   "start": 23.781,
   "end": 36.923,
   "pause": 0.85
  },
  {
   "text": "Four people had been near the prize table at the time: Hedley Truscott, Kerensa Hale, Wenna Polglaze and Tamsin Trevelyan. Exactly one of them took the cake.",
   "start": 37.773,
   "end": 48.119,
   "pause": 0.85
  },
  {
   "text": "Agnes Bell, who was running the game, asked each of them to tell her two things, by the rules of the night.",
   "start": 48.969,
   "end": 55.113,
   "pause": 0.85
  },
  {
   "text": "Hedley said, \"I didn't take the cake. Kerensa took it.\"",
   "start": 55.963,
   "end": 59.313,
   "pause": 0.85
  },
  {
   "text": "Kerensa said, \"I didn't take the cake. Wenna took it.\"",
   "start": 60.163,
   "end": 63.363,
   "pause": 0.85
  },
  {
   "text": "Wenna said, \"I didn't take the cake. Hedley took it.\"",
   "start": 64.213,
   "end": 67.285,
   "pause": 0.85
  },
  {
   "text": "Tamsin said, \"I didn't take the cake. And it wasn't Wenna.\"",
   "start": 68.135,
   "end": 71.633,
   "pause": 0.85
  },
  {
   "text": "Agnes smiled. She loves Truth and Fib Night.",
   "start": 72.483,
   "end": 75.47,
   "pause": 0.85
  },
  {
   "text": "Here are the statements again. Hedley: I didn't take it, Kerensa took it. Kerensa: I didn't take it, Wenna took it. Wenna: I didn't take it, Hedley took it. Tamsin: I didn't take it, it wasn't Wenna. Each person told exactly one truth and one fib.",
   "start": 76.32,
   "end": 92.939,
   "pause": 1.1
  },
  {
   "text": "Can you solve it? Who took the chocolate cake?",
   "start": 94.039,
   "end": 96.556,
   "pause": 1.2
  },
  {
   "text": "Think about it.",
   "start": 97.756,
   "end": 98.78,
   "pause": 0.9
  },
  {
   "text": "Take a moment, or pause here if you are listening. When you are ready, the solution follows.",
   "start": 99.68,
   "end": 104.907,
   "pause": 4.5
  },
  {
   "text": "The Solution.",
   "start": 109.407,
   "end": 110.431,
   "pause": 1.1
  },
  {
   "text": "Tamsin Trevelyan took the cake.",
   "start": 111.531,
   "end": 113.387,
   "pause": 0.85
  },
  {
   "text": "Each person said I didn't take the cake, and then one more thing. Anyone who is innocent is telling the truth with their first statement, so their second statement must be the fib. The one who took the cake is fibbing with the first statement, so their second statement must be true.",
   "start": 114.237,
   "end": 130.621,
   "pause": 0.85
  },
  {
   "text": "Suppose Hedley took it. Then Wenna's second statement, Hedley took it, would be true, while her first, I didn't take it, would also be true. Two truths breaks the rule. So it wasn't Hedley.",
   "start": 131.471,
   "end": 143.119,
   "pause": 0.85
  },
  {
   "text": "In the same way, if Kerensa took it, Hedley would be telling two truths. And if Wenna took it, Kerensa would be telling two truths. So it wasn't Kerensa or Wenna either.",
   "start": 143.969,
   "end": 154.166,
   "pause": 0.85
  },
  {
   "text": "That leaves Tamsin. Her first statement, I didn't take the cake, is the fib. Her second, it wasn't Wenna, is true. Everyone else's second statement is a fib. It all fits.",
   "start": 155.016,
   "end": 166.216,
   "pause": 0.85
  },
  {
   "text": "Tamsin laughed and fetched the cake from under the stage. She had hidden it there, she said, so that she could claim she had told the best fib of the night. Agnes agreed that it had been a very good one, and the cake was shared out among everybody in the hall.",
   "start": 167.066,
   "end": 181.978,
   "pause": 0.0
  }
 ],
